codex
I’ve confirmed the reviewer’s central race: multiple actor calls can interleave while socket readiness is awaited, so the same outbound prefix can be submitted twice, and channel pointers are retained across those suspension points. I’m fixing this at the ownership boundaries: a single queued socket-progress path, no pointer reuse after an `await`, explicit pending-operation accounting, and bounded timeout/cancellation ownership.
