+# TASK-260715-1ozsb6 results
+
+## Delivered
+
+- Added the named `ReluxTunnelLibSSH2Adapter` target as the only Swift target importing `ReluxLibSSH2`; `ReluxTunnelCore` remains candidate-neutral.
+- Implemented the pinned static libssh2/OpenSSL session adapter: custom bounded send/receive callbacks, nonblocking EAGAIN progress, injected socket readiness, async external signing, pre-auth raw host-key policy, approved algorithm enforcement, public-key auth, direct-tcpip, exec, exec/stdin upload with concurrent drains, manual/byte/time client rekey, server-rekey protocol driving, forced keepalive global requests, typed privacy-safe errors, available metrics, allocator hooks, and bounded cleanup.
+- Wired the factory into the macOS provider configuration and dependency-injected harness registration. The harness linkage smoke keeps the static candidate in the release link graph. iOS provider graphs remain unchanged per scope.
+- Consumer receive-window credit, RFC channel-open reason taxonomy, exact exec-exit presence and `coreDumped`, and deep rekey/keepalive observability are explicitly `unsupported` and traced to `TASK-260728-3cveay`. No deferred value is inferred, hard-coded, or parsed from engine prose.
+
+## Review rework
+
+- Serialized socket progress behind one queued owner. Forced overlapping service calls now prove exact-once partial writes and maximum socket-write concurrency of one.
+- Tracked channel pointer users across suspension. One read per channel stream is enforced; queued writes reserve against the per-channel cap; cancel/reset/close marks a typed disposition, waits for pending users, and then frees. Connect, channel-open, session-operation, and teardown drain paths are likewise serialized.
+- Applied the overall upload deadline and source chunk bound. Replaced the structured timeout race that waited for a non-cooperative cancelled child with a prompt cancellation/timeout race. External signer tasks are explicitly tracked, notification-driven, cancelled, and joined during teardown.
+- Applied `allowedConsecutiveMisses` to automatic keepalive failures before connection-fatal teardown. Preserved the active connect phase before teardown and populated timeout/cancellation counters plus pending-open/read/write and queued-byte gauges.
+- Added regressions for concurrent bridge service, signer join, resolution timeout phase/counter cleanup, and twenty repeated connect-cancel cycles. The focused adapter suite now has 11 passing tests.
+
+## Validation evidence
+
+- `swift-format lint --recursive --strict Package.swift Sources Tests`: exit 0.
+- `git diff --check`: exit 0.
+- `swift test --filter LibSSH2BridgeTests`: exit 0; 11 tests passed.
+- `make validate-core`: exit 0; boundary/dependency checks, 349 tests in 30 suites, and `swift build` passed.
+- `make validate-libssh2`: exit 0; pinned static extension-safe artifact, public fork APIs, real client/server rekey, post-rekey channel, and reply-correlated global-request paths passed. Its printed `count=-43` line is the intentional injected socket-failure case.
+- `make test-libssh2-source-gates`: exit 0; tampered sources fail before extraction or patching.
+- `make native-apple-matrix`: exit 0; Apple schemes plus dual-architecture extension-safe macOS provider/harness builds passed, and the stripped release harness contains HEV plus hidden libssh2 rekey linkage.
+
+## Explicit red/deferred evidence
+
+The four M3-owned exact semantics remain `unsupported`, not green. Live Swift-adapter SSH fixtures are intentionally not claimed because the task input assigns those fixtures to `TASK-260715-39xz9g`, common cross-engine conformance to `TASK-260715-2d3g5e`, and the functional/rekey matrix to `TASK-260715-1u2vpc`. This outcome proves adapter implementation, bounded loopback seams, pinned-engine behavior, packaging, and Apple-target conformance without fabricating downstream selection evidence.
